message: >-
  You are not required to cite EquWord simply for using it, but a citation would
  be appreciated. If you choose to cite it, use the all-version Concept DOI and
  state the version used. Sharing the licensed software remains subject to the
  attribution conditions of CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; see LICENSE.txt.
title: "EquWord: Equation Conversion and Formatting for Microsoft Word"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cho
    given-names: Gyeongcheol
version: 1.0.1
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23935877"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
url: "https://github.com/PsycheMatrica/EquWord"
abstract: >-
  A Microsoft Word VBA template for converting supported LaTeX to editable
  native equations and applying document-specific notation and equation-layout
  choices. EquWord.dotm provides nine EquWord_ commands for desktop Word on
  Windows and Mac, including native equation formatting, selective reformatting
  and platform-specific access to reporting information.
